{"name":"She Loves Pink","hex":"#e39b96","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"she","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sheko."]},{"part":"Pronoun","definitions":["The female (typically) person or animal previously mentioned or implied.","A ship or boat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/she"},{"term":"loves","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of love"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of love"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loves"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Love's","blocks":[{"text":"Love's Travel Stops, doing business as Love's, is an American family owned-and-operated chain of more than 670 travel stops in 42 states in the United States. The company is privately owned and headquartered in Oklahoma City. Love's ranked No. 15 on the 2025 Forbes list of America's largest private companies. Love's has two primary kinds of stores: country stores and travel stops. Country stores are fueling stations with a convenience store attached. The larger travel stops are located along highways and offer additional amenities such as food from restaurant chains such as Arby's, Bojangles, Burger King, Chester's, Dunkin' Donuts, McDonald's, Taco John's, Subway, Wendy's, Hardee's/Carl's Jr., truck parking spaces, showers and laundry. The company started adding RV hookups and RV Stops in 2022. Love's had more than 40,000 employees in 2023."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Love%27s_Travel_Stop_%28Bushnell%2C_Fla.%29_%2849417678437%29.jpg/330px-Love%27s_Travel_Stop_%28Bushnell%2C_Fla.%29_%2849417678437%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love's","wikidata":"Q1872496"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg/500px-Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg/1280px-Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg/500px-Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Love's Travel Stops fuel island off Interstate 40 in Choctaw, Oklahoma","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALove's_in_Choctaw.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Love%27s_gas_station.jpg/500px-Love%27s_gas_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Love%27s_gas_station.jpg/1280px-Love%27s_gas_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Love%27s_gas_station.jpg/500px-Love%27s_gas_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wi